 "notes": "AxionPhoton g_agamma 95%-credible upper limit from a search of the SuperMAG magnetometer network for the Earth-as-transducer axion DM magnetic-field signal (Fig. 1, Sec. III/App. C). Traced the light-blue 'This work, smoothed' curve (sliding average of the exclusion limit; the dark-blue 'This work' curve is the raw spiky frequency-by-frequency limit fluctuating >2x locally). Coordinates recovered from vector figure ep/axion_limit.pdf via get_drawings, calibrated on major tick marks (x: 250 px/decade, 10^-17 eV at x=209; y: 66.53 px/decade, 10^-8 GeV^-1 at y=73.21). Mass range ~2.5e-18 to 6.65e-17 eV (plot left frame at 2.48e-18). Assumes axion is all DM at rho_DM=0.3 GeV/cm^3 (stated in text/Fig.1 caption). Strongest smoothed limit ~6.5e-11 GeV^-1 near 3.5e-17 eV, comparable to CAST, matching the paper's stated mean limit of 6.5e-11 GeV^-1. Curve turns up sharply at both ends (edge/noise effects). CAST and SN1987A comparison curves in Fig.1 are external, not reported.",
